        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs have abandoned patience for a bold, money-heavy overhaul, turning their season's disappointment - 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points - into a springboard for aggressive roster construction. <strong>Two-time Stanley Cup champion Sergei Bobrovsky has signed a three-year, $21 million contract</strong>, instantly reshaping the crease alongside Anthony Stolarz in a tandem that backstopped Florida to glory in 2024. The 37-year-old, now wearing No. 72 after a gracious swap with top prospect Gavin McKenna, believes he could become the NHL's best goalie ever, while GM John Chayka's whirlwind moves - adding Duhaime, Raddysh, and Nick Paul - signal a team desperate to climb from last to contender. <strong>Next season's crease battle and the impact of McKenna's development will define whether this high-stakes gamble pays off</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 3, 2026"
